For each representation and dataset we count two quantities. A constant feature takes one value in every molecule of the dataset, and a near-constant feature takes one value in at least 95\% of the molecules, so that the near-constant count includes the constant features. The counts use all molecules of each dataset and the same feature matrices as the main experiments. The datasets are hERG $K_i$, Caco-2, LogD and QM9, together with MDR1--MDCK efflux, human liver microsome (HLM) clearance, rat liver microsome (RLM) clearance and the Lhasa hERG blocker training set. On each dataset we count its base representations, together with the MACCS keys wherever they were computed.

